 "intro": "Near Baecula in southern Spain, 208 BC. Hasdrubal Barca is camped on a plateau with two terraces. You are Publius Cornelius Scipio, a year after the capture of New Carthage.",
 "debrief": "In Polybius’s account, Scipio’s light troops drove the Carthaginian skirmishers off the lower terrace while Laelius and Scipio climbed the flanks of the plateau. Hasdrubal, seeing the danger, withdrew with his treasure, elephants and much of his army, and soon marched for Italy, where he was killed at the Metaurus. Scipio took the camp and many prisoners, and freed Masinissa’s nephew. He refused the Spaniards’ offer to call him king. The other choices are what-ifs.",
